  "id": "f5c2aaa7-215a-5b19-bbb0-8d34080bcbc0",
  "slug": "good-new-orleans-creole-gumbo",
  "name": "Good New Orleans Creole Gumbo",
  "recipe_type": "soup",
  "brief_description": "Traditional Creole gumbo made with roux, shrimp, sausage, and crabmeat. Delicious served over hot cooked rice.",
  "cuisine": "Creole",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Gather all ingredients."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Make the roux: Whisk together flour and 3/4 cup bacon drippings in a large, heavy saucepan over medium-low heat until smooth. Cook roux, whisking constantly, until it turns a rich mahogany brown color. This can take 20 to 30 minutes; watch heat carefully and whisk constantly or roux will burn. Remove from heat; continue whisking until mixture stops cooking."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Make the gumbo: Place celery, onion, green bell pepper, and garlic into the work bowl of a food processor, and pulse until all vegetables are very finely chopped."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Stir vegetables into roux, and mix in sliced sausage. Cook over medium-low heat, stirring constantly, until vegetables are tender, 10 to 15 minutes. Remove from heat and set aside."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Combine water and beef bouillon cubes in a large Dutch oven or soup pot and bring to a boil over medium-high heat. Stir until bouillon cubes dissolve, then whisk roux mixture into the boiling water."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Reduce heat to a simmer and mix in sugar, salt, hot pepper sauce, Cajun seasoning, bay leaves, thyme, stewed tomatoes, and tomato sauce. Simmer soup over low heat for 1 hour; mix in 2 teaspoons of file gumbo powder at the 45-minute mark."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Meanwhile, melt 2 tablespoons bacon drippings in a skillet over medium heat. Add okra and vinegar and cook for 15 minutes; remove okra with a slotted spoon, and stir into the simmering gumbo."
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "text": "Mix in crabmeat, shrimp, and Worcestershire sauce, and simmer until flavors have blended, 45 more minutes. Stir in 2 more teaspoons of file gumbo powder just before serving."
    },
    {
      "position": 9,
      "text": "Serve hot and enjoy!"
    }
  ],
  "servings": 20,
